      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "Implement `deepClone(value)`, which returns a full, independent copy of `value` — for arrays and plain objects, nested arrays/objects must also be copied recursively, not just shallowly referenced, so mutating the clone never affects the original (and vice versa). The input may contain circular references (an object that, through some chain of properties, refers back to itself); the clone must handle this without infinitely recursing.",
