      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "Implement an `InfiniteList` component that renders a paginated feed using `FlatList`. Each time the user scrolls near the bottom, the component should fetch the next page from a provided `fetchPage(pageNumber)` function, append the results to the currently rendered list, and show a loading spinner in the list footer while a fetch is in flight. The component must never trigger two overlapping fetches for the same page, and must stop requesting more pages once the data source reports there's nothing left. This is a single reusable component, not a full app screen — assume the caller owns the actual API/data-fetching implementation and only hands `InfiniteList` a `fetchPage` function plus a way to render each item.",
      "input": "`fetchPage: (pageNumber: number) => Promise<{ items: T[]; hasMore: boolean }>` —; `renderItem: (item: T) => ReactElement` — how to render a single row.; `keyExtractor: (item: T) => string` — stable unique key per item.",
