      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "Given an integer array `nums`, return all unique triplets `[nums[i], nums[j], nums[k]]` such that `i != j`, `i != k`, and `j != k`, and `nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] === 0`. Notice that the solution set must not contain duplicate triplets.",
      "input": "`nums`: an array of integers",
      "output": "An array of arrays of integers, where each inner array is a unique 3-element triplet `[a, b, c]` that sums to 0.",
