      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "Given an array of distinct positive integers `candidates` and a target integer `target`, return all unique combinations of `candidates` that sum to exactly `target`. The same number may be chosen from `candidates` an unlimited number of times. Return the combinations in any order; a combination is a set of numbers regardless of order (so `[2,2,3]` and `[2,3,2]` count as the same combination and should only appear once).",
