      "problemStatement": "There are `piles` of bananas, `piles[i]` bananas in the `i`-th pile. Koko can eat at most one pile per hour, at a chosen constant speed `k` bananas per hour: if a pile has fewer than `k` bananas left, she finishes that pile in that hour and doesn't start another; if it has `k` or more, she eats exactly `k` and the rest remain for a later hour. Given `h` hours until the piles must all be finished, return the minimum integer eating speed `k` that lets Koko finish all piles within `h` hours.",
