      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "Given the `root` of a binary tree, flatten the tree into a \"linked list\": - The \"linked list\" should use the same `TreeNode` class where the `right` child pointer points to the next node in the list and the `left` child pointer is always `null`. - The \"linked list\" should be in the same order as a **pre-order traversal** of the binary tree. Solve it **in-place** with $O(1)$ extra space.",
      "input": "Parameters as specified",
      "output": "Result as specified",
      "constraints": [
        "Standard time and space bounds apply."
      ],
      "examples": [],
