      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "You have a graph of `n` nodes labeled from `0` to `n - 1`. You are given an integer `n` and a list of `edges` where `edges[i] = [a_i, b_i]` indicates that there is an undirected edge between nodes `a_i` and `b_i` in the graph. Return `true` if the edges of the given graph make up a **valid tree**, and `false` otherwise.",
      "input": "`n`: `number` — number of vertices; `edges`: `number[][]` — 2D array of undirected edges",
      "output": "`boolean` — `true` if graph is a valid tree, `false` otherwise",
      "constraints": [
        "`1 <= n <= 2000`",
        "`0 <= edges.length <= 5000`",
        "`edges[i].length == 2`",
        "`0 <= a_i, b_i < n`"
      ],
