    "detail": {
      "id": "q1628",
      "questionNumber": "Q6592",
      "title": "Surrounded Regions (Boundary Connected Graph DFS/BFS)",
      "difficulty": "Medium",
      "companies": [
        "Amazon",
        "Meta",
        "Google",
        "Microsoft",
        "Apple"
      ],
      "frequency": 5,
      "category": "graph",
      "concepts": [
        "graph",
        "dfs",
        "bfs",
        "matrix",
        "boundary-flood-fill"
      ],
      "solved": false,
      "attempted": false,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "questionType": "coding",
      "problemStatement": "Given an `m x n` matrix `board` containing `'X'` and `'O'`, **capture all regions that are 4-directionally surrounded by `'X'`**. A region is captured by flipping all `'O'`s into `'X'`s in that surrounded region. Note: - An `'O'` cell is on the **border** of the matrix if it is in the first row, last row, first column, or last column. - Any `'O'` connected to a border `'O'` **cannot be surrounded** and will **never be flipped** into `'X'`.",
      "input": "`board`: `string[][]` — 2D matrix of `'X'` and `'O'` characters",
      "output": "Modifies `board` in-place (void return)",
      "constraints": [
        "`m == board.length`",
        "`n == board[i].length`",
        "`1 <= m, n <= 200`",
        "`board[i][j]` is `'X'` or `'O'`."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "input": "board = [[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"O\",\"O\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"X\",\"O\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"O\",\"X\",\"X\"]]",
          "output": "[[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"O\",\"X\",\"X\"]]",
          "explanation": "Inner `'O'`s captured; bottom `'O'` at border is preserved"
        },
        {
          "input": "board = [[\"X\"]]",
          "output": "[[\"X\"]]",
          "explanation": "1x1 grid"
        }
      ],
      "edgeCases": [
        {
          "case": "Board with no border `'O'`s",
          "expected": "all inner `'O'`s are captured!"
        }
      ],
      "functionName": "solve",
      "isClassBased": false,
      "sampleTests": []
    },
    "hints": {
      "hints": [
        "**Reverse Boundary Flood-Fill Strategy**:",
        "Any `'O'` connected to a border `'O'` CANNOT be captured.",
        "Step 1: Traverse all 4 borders (top, bottom, left, right)."
      ]
    },
    "solution": {
      "algorithm": "**Pattern:** Boundary-Connected Sentinel Flood-Fill  \n**Core Insight:** Starting DFS flood-fill from border `'O'` nodes temporarily renames un-capturable regions to `'E'`, leaving true surrounded inner regions exposed for single-pass replacement.",
      "dryRun": "`board = [[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"O\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"]]`:\n- Border check: No border `'O'`s exist.\n- Grid pass: Inner `(1, 1) ('O')` is surrounded -> flipped to `'X'`.\n- Result: `[[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"],[\"X\",\"X\",\"X\"]]`.",
      "javascriptSolution": "function solve(board) {\n  const m = board.length;\n  const n = board[0].length;\n\n  function dfs(r, c) {\n    if (r < 0 || r >= m || c < 0 || c >= n || board[r][c] !== 'O') {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    board[r][c] = 'E'; // Mark as Escaped/Uncaptured\n\n    dfs(r + 1, c);\n    dfs(r - 1, c);\n    dfs(r, c + 1);\n    dfs(r, c - 1);\n  }\n\n  // 1. Mark border-connected 'O's with 'E'\n  for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n    dfs(0, c);        // Top border\n    dfs(m - 1, c);    // Bottom border\n  }\n\n  for (let r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n    dfs(r, 0);        // Left border\n    dfs(r, n - 1);    // Right border\n  }\n\n  // 2. Flip surrounded 'O's to 'X', restore 'E's back to 'O'\n  for (let r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n      if (board[r][c] === 'O') {\n        board[r][c] = 'X';\n      } else if (board[r][c] === 'E') {\n        board[r][c] = 'O';\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
      "typescriptSolution": "function solve(board: string[][]): void {\n  const m = board.length;\n  const n = board[0].length;\n\n  function dfs(r: number, c: number): void {\n    if (r < 0 || r >= m || c < 0 || c >= n || board[r][c] !== 'O') {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    board[r][c] = 'E';\n\n    dfs(r + 1, c);\n    dfs(r - 1, c);\n    dfs(r, c + 1);\n    dfs(r, c - 1);\n  }\n\n  for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n    dfs(0, c);\n    dfs(m - 1, c);\n  }\n\n  for (let r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n    dfs(r, 0);\n    dfs(r, n - 1);\n  }\n\n  for (let r = 0; r < m; r++) {\n    for (let c = 0; c < n; c++) {\n      if (board[r][c] === 'O') {\n        board[r][c] = 'X';\n      } else if (board[r][c] === 'E') {\n        board[r][c] = 'O';\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
      "timeComplexity": "`O(M * N)` — constant number of passes over $M \\times N$ cells.",
      "spaceComplexity": "`O(M * N)` — call stack space in worst-case grid flood-fill.",
      "commonMistakes": [
        "Initiating DFS from inner `'O'` cells forward, requiring complex tracking of whether any branch reaches a border before deciding to flip."
      ],
      "followUpQuestions": [
        "How does Pacific Atlantic Water Flow compare in reverse shoreline boundary traversal logic?"
      ],
      "similarQuestions": [
        "Number of Islands",
        "Pacific Atlantic Water Flow"
      ]
    }
