      "deepExplanation": "When modules form a cycle, the engine breaks the loop by returning a partially-populated module for whichever side is still being evaluated when the cycle is detected. In ESM, thanks to live bindings, the importing side sees an initial `undefined`/TDZ-like state for values not yet assigned, but the binding updates automatically once the exporting module finishes running.",
