      "deepExplanation": "`this` is determined by the call-site, not where the function was defined. When a method is detached from its object — passed as a callback, destructured, or reassigned to a variable — it loses its implicit binding and `this` falls back to undefined (strict mode) or the global object.",
      "productionExample": "```js\nFollow standard modern practices.\n```",
