      "deepExplanation": "The `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(x))` trick deep-clones only JSON-safe data — it silently drops `undefined`, functions, and symbols, converts `Date` objects into strings (losing the Date type), and throws on circular references. The structured clone algorithm (used by `structuredClone()`, `postMessage`, and IndexedDB) correctly preserves `Date`, `Map`, `Set`, `RegExp`, typed arrays, and circular references, but still cannot clone functions or DOM nodes.",
      "productionExample": "```js\nFollow standard modern practices.\n```",
      "bestPractices": [
        "Apply modern standards and clear conventions.",
        "Prefer explicit intent over implicit coercion or hidden side effects."
      ],
