      "deepExplanation": "JavaScript implicitly converts operand types to make an operation valid — the `+` operator prefers string concatenation if either operand is a string (or converts via `toPrimitive` with a 'default' hint), while `-`, `*`, `/` always coerce both operands toward numbers. Objects are converted to primitives via `valueOf()`/`toString()` before these rules apply.",
