      "deepExplanation": "A `WeakMap` only accepts objects as keys, and holds a 'weak' reference to them — if a key object has no other references anywhere in the program, it (and its associated value) is eligible for garbage collection, and the entry silently disappears from the WeakMap. It's also non-enumerable — there's no way to iterate or get the size of a WeakMap.",
